            "defect_found": false,
            "unresolved_central_mathematical_gap": null,
            "full_claim": "For every prime p, every field k of characteristic p, and every compact Lie group G whose component group is not p-nilpotent, with X=(BG)^wedge_p completed before looping and R=C_*(Omega X;k), the canonical k-cellularization map Gamma_k R -> R induces zero H_n for every integer n.",
            "supported_intermediate_claim": "Every A-linear map from Loc_A(k) to A induces zero homology if k is proxy-small and H_*(A) is an infinite-dimensional Koszul graded Hopf algebra.",
